# Next.js app (apps/web)

## Stack

Next.js App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Zod. Low-dependency; server components by default where appropriate.

## Required routes (do not remove without product decision)

`/`, `/sources`, `/sources/[id]`, `/claims`, `/claims/[id]`, `/tensions`, `/tensions/[id]`, `/decisions`, `/decisions/[id]`, `/outputs`, `/outputs/[id]`, `/review`, `/changes`, `/settings/vault-sync`.

## UX stance

Calm, rigorous, inspectable. **Not** chat-first or graph-first. Primary value: inbox/review, provenance panels, status, and operational outputs.

## Implementation habits

- Keep feature logic in `features/<domain>/` (components, server, types).
- Validate inputs with Zod on server boundaries.
- Preserve provenance in UI copy and data fetching (link evidence, sources, review events).
- See [cursor-execution-brief.md](cursor-execution-brief.md) for step-by-step delivery expectations.
